      "body": "# What does this PR do?\n\nFixes #10887\n\n## Summary\nWhen transparent images (`RGBA`, `LA`, `PA`, or palette `P` with transparency metadata in `image.info`) are converted directly using `convert(\"RGB\")`, Pillow discards the alpha channel without compositing over a background. In PNG assets, transparent background pixels typically store `(0, 0, 0)` under the alpha mask, causing transparent regions to turn solid black. For diagrams, math charts, document scans, and UI screenshots featuring dark drawings or black text on a transparent background, this turns the entire image black-on-black and renders features invisible to vision-language models.\n\nThis PR introduces a `to_rgb()` helper that detects transparency, composites transparent images onto a clean white background (`(255, 255, 255)`), and returns RGB:\n- Checks if `image.mode in (\"RGBA\", \"LA\", \"PA\") or \"transparency\" in image.info`\n- Converts to `\"RGBA\"`, pastes onto a white `RGB` canvas using `image.getchannel(\"A\")` as alpha mask\n- Leaves non-transparent images or standard RGB images untouched\n- Applied in `BasePlugin._preprocess_image` (used across all multimodal plugins and vLLM engine) and `_process_request` in `src/llamafactory/api/chat.py`\n- Added unit tests in `tests/data/test_mm_plugin.py` covering RGBA, LA, palette with transparency, and RGB passthrough.\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] Did you read the [contributor guideline](https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory/blob/main/.github/CONTRIBUTING.md)?\n- [x] Did you write any new necessary tests?",
